                <pb facs="0737" n="643" sameAs="frus:frus1930v03/pg643"/>

                <note rend="inline" type="source">817.0131/10: Telegram</note>
                <head><hi rendition="#italic">The Minister in Nicaragua</hi> (<hi rendition="#italic">Hanna</hi>) <hi rendition="#italic"
                        >to the Secretary of State</hi></head>
                <opener><dateline rendition="#float-right"><placeName><hi rendition="#small-caps"
                                >Managua</hi></placeName>, <date calendar="gregorian"
                            when="1930-07-02T21:00:00-05:45">July 2, 1930—9
                        p.m.</date><lb/>[Received July 3—12:38 a.m.]</dateline></opener>
                <p>[81?] My telegram No. 77, June 30, 7 p.m. President Moncada has just given me
                    legal citations supporting his plan to make the amendments to the electoral law
                    by Executive decree, with the request that Captain Johnson and I confer
                    informally with members of the Supreme Court and then advise him as to our
                    conclusions. We will do so unless you instruct otherwise but we will report our
                    conclusions to you before communicating them to President Moncada. Details by
                    air mail.</p>
                <closer><signed><hi rendition="#small-caps">Hanna</hi></signed></closer>
            </div>
        </body>
